{
  "name": "Audio Textures",
  "description": "Audio textures demo: a synthwave visualiser built from the three audio textures. The spectrum (u_spectrum) as a slowly spinning ring of polar bars with falling peak caps around a striped retro sun, the waveform (u_waveform) as a trigger-aligned oscilloscope line on the horizon, and the spectrogram (an Audio Texture node, 256 bins x 4 s ring buffer) as a perspective floor that scrolls toward you, lows down the middle, with a grid that moves with the history. HDR composite, two-level bloom through Feedback render targets, ACES tonemap, vignette and grain. Mic / file / tab audio drive it live; the metronome plays a deterministic synthetic mix (headless renders); audio off = flat. Parameters panel: horizon, ring centre / radius / bar length / bars / spin / brightness, wave height / thickness / brightness, floor spread / glow, colours, bloom, exposure.",
  "version": "1.0",
  "timestamp": "2026-10-25T13:18:06.323Z",
  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 80,
        "y": -398,
        "data": {
          "text": "# Audio Textures\nA synthwave visualiser built from the three audio textures: the spectrum as a ring of polar bars around a striped sun, the waveform as an oscilloscope line on the horizon, and the spectrogram (the last 4 s of spectra) as a floor that scrolls toward you in perspective, lows down the middle. HDR composite, two-level bloom, ACES tonemap.\nPlay music: open the audio menu \u2192 Mic, a file or tab audio. With the metronome it plays a deterministic synthetic mix (kick, bass line, Am-F-C-G chords, snare, hats), so it also renders headless; with audio off the bars, line and floor go flat.\n## How it is wired\n- Circular Spectrum and Waveform Line read the global u_spectrum / u_waveform (no wiring needed).\n- Floor UV maps the floor to spectrogram coordinates (x = time, y = frequency) and feeds an Audio Texture (kind spectrogram) uv input; its value is the floor brightness.\n- Bright pass \u2192 two Feedback render targets (320x200, 96x60) \u2192 blur \u2192 added back.\n## Tweak it\nPress P: Scene, Ring, Waveform, Floor, Colour and Post settings.",
          "width": 440,
          "height": 430,
          "color": "orange"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 80,
        "y": -78,
        "data": {
          "text": "## Spectrum ring\nCircular Spectrum around the ring centre, slowly spinning (mirrored: lows at the top). Its mask / cap / level / ring outputs are coloured in Audio Compose.",
          "width": 300,
          "height": 110,
          "color": "pink"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 2,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 80,
        "y": -64,
        "data": {
          "text": "## Waveform horizon\nWaveform Line centred on the horizon (uv.y = horizon * 0.5 + 0.5): a trigger-aligned oscilloscope.",
          "width": 300,
          "height": 96,
          "color": "green"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 3,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 80,
        "y": -88,
        "data": {
          "text": "## Spectrogram floor\nFloor UV \u2192 Audio Texture (spectrogram, 256 bins, 4 s) uv. The newest row is at the bottom edge, the oldest at the horizon; the grid scrolls with the history.",
          "width": 320,
          "height": 120,
          "color": "violet"
        }
      },
      {
